          "id": "1775301128779",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1775301128781_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "Use this data source for the production exception summary:\n{{$context.$nodes.FETCH_PRODUCTION_EXCEPTIONS_RELATED_TO_MATERIAL.$output.items}}\n\nUse this data source for the shift summary:\n{{$context.$nodes.FETCH_SHIFT_SUMMARIES.$output.items}}\n\nOutput Contract (MUST FOLLOW EXACTLY)\n\nRender only the content. Do not add any main heading. The panel already provides the heading.\n\nRequired order:\n1) Production exception subsection\n2) Shift Summary subsection\n3) Table\n\n\nExact output structure:\n\nProduction exception\n<summary paragraph>\n\nShift Summary\n<summary paragraph>\n\n<table>\n\nUpdate Material Quantity\n\n----------------------------------------\nProduction exception subsection rules:\n----------------------------------------\n- Heading must be exactly: Production exception\n- Write one short paragraph (2–4 lines)\n- Use:\n  {{$context.$nodes.FETCH_PRODUCTION_EXCEPTIONS_RELATED_TO_MATERIAL.$output.items}}\n- Mention:\n  - total number of exceptions\n  - severity pattern if visible\n  - impacted item/work order\n- Do not print JSON\n- Do not list records\n- If none:\n  No production exceptions were found for the selected item.\n\n----------------------------------------\nShift Summary subsection rules:\n----------------------------------------\n- Heading must be exactly: Shift Summary\n- Write one short paragraph (2–4 lines)\n- Use only NoteText from:\n  {{$context.$nodes.FETCH_SHIFT_SUMMARIES.$output.items}}\n\nSTRICT MATCH RULE:\n- Read only the NoteText field of each item.\n- Ignore every other field.\n- The shift summary may be written ONLY if NoteText contains the exact literal value:\n  {{$context.$nodes.PARSE_ACTION_CODE.$output.result.data.MaterialItemNumber}}\n- Match must be case-insensitive.\n- Match must be a literal substring match only.\n- Do not use semantic matching.\n- Do not use fuzzy matching.\n- Do not use partial matching.\n- Do not infer a match from related materials, work orders, shift context, exceptions, or production issues.\n- Do not substitute similar codes.\n- Do not treat MFG-PL-PROD5 as a match for MFG-PL-COMP6 or any other code.\n\nWHEN A MATCH EXISTS:\n- Summarize only the matching NoteText content.\n- Mention:\n  - the exact material item number\n  - the shift context\n  - the issue, exception, variance, or action mentioned\n- Keep it to 2–4 lines.\n- Do not print raw JSON.\n- Do not list multiple items separately.\n- Do not echo field names.\n- Do not mention any other material code.\n\nWHEN NO MATCH EXISTS:\n- Output exactly:\n  No shift summary mentions were found for the selected material.\n\n\n\nRender the values from materialDetailedInsight\n\nYou are a JSON API that generates UI widgets.\n\nForget previous responses. This is a stateless request.\n\nSTRICT RULES:\n\nOutput ONLY valid JSON\nDo NOT include text, explanation, or markdown\nDo NOT render a table\nDo NOT print raw JSON as text\nDo NOT wrap JSON in quotes\nResponse must be directly parseable\n\n\nalways render the data in a multiRecordWidget (Critical)\nWIDGET:\nmultiRecordWidget\n\nYour input is {{$context.$nodes.PARSE_ACTION_CODE.$output.result.data}}\n- Do not print raw JSON.\nDisplay columns in this format:\nColumns:\nWork Definition Name | Item Number | Operation Sequence-Name | Material | Required Quantity | Average Issued Quantity | Material Variance\n\nMapping:\n- Work Definition Name -> WorkDefinitionName\n- Item Number -> ItemNumber\n- Operation Sequence-Name -> OperationSequenceNumber-OperationName\n- Material -> MaterialItemNumber\n- Required -> QuantityPlannedQtyPerProduct\n- Average -> Issued QuantityActualQtyPerProduct\n- Material Variance -> MaterialVariance\n\n\n\nApply highlighting for Material Variance:\n- If > 30 → Red {{MaterialVariance}}%\n- If > 20 → Orange {{MaterialVariance}}%\n- If > 10 → Yellow {{MaterialVariance}}%\nMaterial Variance must be displayed as a percentage string.\nAlways append % to the numeric value.\nExample: 26 -> 26%\nDo not remove the percent sign\n\n## Action (per row) — STRICT BINDING (do not mix up)\nActionText: `Material Quantity Update` **ONLY**\n\n**followUpCommand**\n- `ora.Agent({\n  \"actionType\": \"materialQuantityUpdate\",\n  \"data\": {\n    \"WorkDefinitionId\": \"{{$context.$nodes.PARSE_ACTION_CODE.$output.result.data.WorkDefinitionId}}\",\n    \"OrganizationId\": \"{{$context.$nodes.PARSE_ACTION_CODE.$output.result.data.OrganizationId}}\",\n    \"WdOperationMaterialId\": \"{{$context.$nodes.PARSE_ACTION_CODE.$output.result.data.WdOperationMaterialId}}\",\n    \"WorkOrderNumbers\": \"{{$context.$nodes.PARSE_ACTION_CODE.$output.result.data.WorkOrderNumbers}}\",\n    \"ActualQtyPerProduct\": \"{{$context.$nodes.PARSE_ACTION_CODE.$output.result.data.ActualQtyPerProduct}}\",\n    \"PlannedQtyPerProduct\": \"{{$context.$nodes.PARSE_ACTION_CODE.$output.result.data.PlannedQtyPerProduct}}\",\n    \"WorkDefinitionCode\": \"{{$context.$nodes.PARSE_ACTION_CODE.$output.result.data.WorkDefinitionCode}}\",\n    \"WorkDefinitionName\": \"{{$context.$nodes.PARSE_ACTION_CODE.$output.result.data.WorkDefinitionName}}\",\n    \"ItemNumber\": \"{{$context.$nodes.PARSE_ACTION_CODE.$output.result.data.ItemNumber}}\",\n    \"MaterialItemNumber\": \"{{$context.$nodes.PARSE_ACTION_CODE.$output.result.data.MaterialItemNumber}}\"\n  }\n})`\n\n- Do not print raw JSON.\n- **(Display the text exactly as provided, but replace every underscore character `_` with the HTML entity `&#95;`. Do not change anything else or any character other than `_`. Return only the transformed text.)"
