          "id": "1775305790527",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1775305790568_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "Your input is {{$context.$nodes.PARSE_ACTION_CODE.$output.result.data}}\n\nUse this data source for the production exception summary:\n{{$context.$nodes.FETCH_PRODUCTION_EXCEPTIONS.$output}}\n\nUse this data source for the shift summary:\n{{$context.$nodes.FETCH_OPERATOR_NOTES.$output}}\n\nTable Title: Resource Usage Variation-Detailed Insights\n\nOutput Contract\n\nRender only the content. Do not add any main heading. The panel already provides the heading.\n\nRequired order:\n1) Production exception subsection\n2) Shift Summary subsection\n3) Table\n\nExact output structure:\n\nProduction exception\n<summary paragraph>\n\nShift Summary\n<summary paragraph>\n\n<table>\n\nResource Usage Update\n\n----------------------------------------\nProduction exception subsection rules:\n----------------------------------------\n- Heading must be exactly: Production exception\n- Write one short paragraph (2–4 lines)\n- Use:\n  {{$context.$nodes.FETCH_PRODUCTION_EXCEPTIONS.$output}}\n- Mention:\n  - total number of exceptions\n  - severity pattern if visible\n  - impacted resource, work definition, or work order if visible\n- Do not print JSON\n- Do not list records\n- If none:\n  No production exceptions were found for the selected resource.\n\n----------------------------------------\nShift Summary subsection rules:\n----------------------------------------\n- Heading must be exactly: Shift Summary\n- Write one short paragraph (2–4 lines)\n- Use only NoteText from:\n  {{$context.$nodes.FETCH_OPERATOR_NOTES.$output}}\n\nSTRICT MATCH RULE:\n- Read only the NoteText field of each item.\n- Ignore every other field.\n- The shift summary may be written ONLY if NoteText contains the exact literal value:\n  {{$context.$nodes.PARSE_ACTION_CODE.$output.result.data.ResourceCode}}\n- Match must be case-insensitive.\n- Match must be a literal substring match only.\n- Do not use semantic matching.\n- Do not use fuzzy matching.\n- Do not use partial matching.\n- Do not infer a match from related materials, work orders, shift context, exceptions, or production issues.\n- Do not substitute similar codes.\n- Do not treat one resource code as a match for any other resource code.\n\nWHEN A MATCH EXISTS:\n- Summarize only the matching NoteText content.\n- Mention:\n  - the exact resource code\n  - the shift context\n  - the issue, exception, variance, or action mentioned\n- Keep it to 2–4 lines.\n- Do not print raw JSON.\n- Do not list multiple items separately.\n- Do not echo field names.\n- Do not mention any other resource code.\n\nWHEN NO MATCH EXISTS:\n- Output exactly:\n  No shift summary mentions were found for the selected resource.\n\nRender the values from resourceDetailedInsight in a table.\n\nDisplay columns in this format:\nWork Definition Name | Item Number | Operation Sequence-Name | Resource | Planned Usage | Average Actual Resource Usage | Resource Variance\n\nMap fields:\n- Work Definition Name -> WorkDefinitionName\n- Item Number -> ItemNumber\n- Operation Sequence-Name -> OperationSequenceNumber-OperationName\n- Resource -> ResourceCode\n- Planned Usage -> PlannedUsagePerProduct\n- Average Actual Resource Usage -> ActualUsagePerProduct\n- Resource Variance -> ResourceVariance\n\nApply highlighting for Resource Variance:\n- If > 30 → Red {{ResourceVariance}}%\n- If > 20 → Orange {{ResourceVariance}}%\n- If > 10 → Yellow {{ResourceVariance}}%\n\nResource Variance must be displayed as a percentage string.\nAlways append % to the numeric value.\nExample: 26 -> 26%\nDo not remove the percent sign.\n\n## Action (per row) — STRICT BINDING (do not mix up)\nActionText: `Resource Usage Update` **ONLY**\n\n**followUpCommand**\n- `ora.Agent({\n  \"actionType\": \"resourceUsageUpdate\",\n  \"data\": {\n    \"WorkDefinitionId\": \"{{$context.$nodes.PARSE_ACTION_CODE.$output.result.data.WorkDefinitionId}}\",\n    \"OrganizationCode\": \"{{$context.$nodes.PARSE_ACTION_CODE.$output.result.data.OrganizationCode}}\",\n    \"OrganizationId\": \"{{$context.$nodes.PARSE_ACTION_CODE.$output.result.data.OrganizationId}}\",\n    \"WorkDefinitionCode\": \"{{$context.$nodes.PARSE_ACTION_CODE.$output.result.data.WorkDefinitionCode}}\",\n    \"WorkDefinitionVersionNumber\": \"{{$context.$nodes.PARSE_ACTION_CODE.$output.result.data.WorkDefinitionVersionNumber}}\",\n    \"WorkMethodCode\": \"{{$context.$nodes.PARSE_ACTION_CODE.$output.result.data.WorkMethodCode}}\",\n    \"ItemNumber\": \"{{$context.$nodes.PARSE_ACTION_CODE.$output.result.data.ItemNumber}}\",\n    \"WorkOrderNumbers\": \"{{$context.$nodes.PARSE_ACTION_CODE.$output.result.data.WorkOrderNumbers}}\",\n    \"OperationSequenceNumber\": \"{{$context.$nodes.PARSE_ACTION_CODE.$output.result.data.OperationSequenceNumber}}\",\n    \"ResourceCode\": \"{{$context.$nodes.PARSE_ACTION_CODE.$output.result.data.ResourceCode}}\",\n    \"ResourceSequenceNumber\": \"{{$context.$nodes.PARSE_ACTION_CODE.$output.result.data.ResourceSequenceNumber}}\",\n    \"PlannedUsagePerProduct\": \"{{$context.$nodes.PARSE_ACTION_CODE.$output.result.data.PlannedUsagePerProduct}}\",\n    \"ActualUsagePerProduct\": \"{{$context.$nodes.PARSE_ACTION_CODE.$output.result.data.ActualUsagePerProduct}}\"\n  }\n})`\n\n- **(Display the text exactly as provided, but replace every underscore character `_` with the HTML entity `&#95;`. Do not change anything else or any character other than `_`. Return only the transformed text.)**"
